# SYNTHESISED to exercise the cross-tier join by resource type: every other
# fixture in this repo carries one tier or the other, never both, so nothing
# renders a joined row where the RPC and UI-hook figures sit side by side.
# This file carries all three join outcomes -- aws_instance in BOTH tiers,
# aws_subnet in the RPC tier only, local_file in the UI tier only. The hclog
# lines follow testdata/provider-rpc.log's "Received downstream response"
# shape; the terraform.ui JSON lines follow testdata/structured-ui.log's
# apply_start/apply_complete shape. Values are invented; no line here is from
# a real run. Every elapsed_seconds is a WHOLE number, as a real log's always
# is: Terraform rounds both endpoints of a resource's timing to the nearest
# second before subtracting them (internal/command/views/hook_json.go), which
# is exactly the resolution gap the types view exists to expose against the
# millisecond-precision RPC tier beside it.
